## Getting Started

### 1 Installation

```bash

# Install the Jac toolchain
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jaseci-labs/jaseci/main/scripts/install.sh | bash

# Individual plugins
jac install byllm        # LLM integration

# (Production deployment & scaling and full-stack web + native-desktop app

#  building ship with the jac binary -- no separate install)
```

This installs the self-contained `jac` binary -- no Python, pip, or uv required.

### 2 Your First Program

Create a file `hello.jac`:

```jac
def greet(name: str) -> str {
    return f"Hello, {name}!";
}

with entry {
    print(greet("World"));
}
```

Run it:

```bash
jac hello.jac
```

Note: `jac` is shorthand for `jac run`.

### 3 Project Structure

```
my_project/
├── jac.toml           # Project configuration
├── main.jac           # Entry point
├── app.jac            # Full-stack entry (jac-client)
├── models/
│   ├── __init__.jac
│   └── user.jac
└── tests/
    └── test_models.jac
```

**File Extensions:**

| Extension | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| `.jac` | Universal Jac code (head module) |
| `.sv.jac`

 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

obj BlueprintSpec {
    has title: str;
    has diagram_type: str;
    has description: str;
    has components: list[str];
    has relationships: list[str];
    has style: str;
}
sem BlueprintSpec = "Structured plan for a diagram to be rendered";
sem BlueprintSpec.title = "Short descriptive title for the diagram";
sem BlueprintSpec.diagram_type = "One of: architecture, sequence, mindmap, entity-relationship, flowchart, state, class, other";
sem BlueprintSpec.description = "1-2 sentence summary of what the diagram shows";
sem BlueprintSpec.components = "List of key shapes or entities to include as nodes";
sem BlueprintSpec.relationships = "Descriptions of how components connect, e.g. 'User sends request to API Gateway'";
sem BlueprintSpec.style = "Color scheme or visual style preferences, e.g. 'blue tones, minimal'";

enum PlannerNextStep {
    DONE = "DONE",
    SYNTHESIZE = "SYNTHESIZE"
